From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: pw4-port <pw4-port@localhost>
Date: Mon, 23 Nov 2026 16:37:38 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] fsl_otp: enable the OCOTP clock before reading the i.MX6SLL
 serial

Every other register access in the driver enables it first. At power-on
the gate happens to be open; after the stock suspend the PW4 handoff
starts from, it is not, and the read stalls the bus.
---
 drivers/char/fsl_otp.c | 6 +++++-
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/char/fsl_otp.c b/drivers/char/fsl_otp.c
index abc147bd..9cda9afc 100644
--- a/drivers/char/fsl_otp.c
+++ b/drivers/char/fsl_otp.c
@@ -582,13 +582,17 @@ static int fsl_otp_probe(struct platform_device *pdev)
 	mutex_init(&otp_mutex);
 
 	/* set system serial from otp */
-	if (fsl_otp->devtype == FSL_OTP_MX6SLL) {
+	if (fsl_otp->devtype == FSL_OTP_MX6SLL && !clk_prepare_enable(otp_clk)) {
+		/* The registers need the OCOTP clock, as everywhere else in this
+		 * driver: at power-on the gate happens to be open, after a stock
+		 * suspend it is not, and a read then stalls the bus. */
 		fsl_otp->set_otp_timing();
 		ret = otp_wait_busy(0);
 		if (!ret) {
 			system_serial_low = __raw_readl(otp_base + HW_OCOTP_CUST_N(1));
 			system_serial_high = __raw_readl(otp_base + HW_OCOTP_CUST_N(2));
 		}
+		clk_disable_unprepare(otp_clk);
 	}
 
 	return 0;
